s","target_id":"bab1-6f12-2313-49c2"},{"link_uuid":"80e6fe8b-91e2-48db-93f8-61d9a470c30b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d13a-45fa-bc11-4c24"},{"link_uuid":"6110469f-baeb-478c-a0e7-bcf202b42a95","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"88cc-f9ff-ed88-4935"},{"link_uuid":"6ff2162c-e9f6-4b73-b8d8-73d256a92333","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2cd9-5cbf-dde8-460a"},{"link_uuid":"2b400e26-0c11-492e-851b-982cccb15c80","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6a74-cebe-b2c2-48d3"},{"link_uuid":"db486034-99ae-46fe-ae1a-782c685cd0b8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"adae-bf10-d8e6-48d9"},{"link_uuid":"6b8049d4-20cc-438b-91a2-11eecaa34a01","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4c45-1878-4550-479d"},{"link_uuid":"790b491b-a5ea-4bb1-8b30-1c73a789eb11","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e5a6-40ab-8231-4a8e"},{"link_uuid":"33b897fb-af0d-45c5-8cce-5984cd2678f0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"655a-b048-6330-4fcc"},{"link_uuid":"a58822d5-1c5e-4e3d-8e5f-45975c0b29ba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8c41-9c0a-ced0-4a35"},{"link_uuid":"c10d37a2-6373-4cde-aaba-a3eab4ba7abd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"149c-1abe-7b79-45db"},{"link_uuid":"6cf86a83-e090-4757-a995-03f467b468c7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"026d-e15b-2565-4468"},{"link_uuid":"2dcd5805-fb2c-4445-b21d-96a1f1b48466","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6c9a-6f7b-7649-4830"},{"link_uuid":"7645e71c-7263-4d85-a603-b8276edac683","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cf5c-9d5a-50e8-4cc1"},{"link_uuid":"124c9093-c777-42e7-ae61-60be946cbbd4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a62c-15f0-a8b7-4856"},{"link_uuid":"d3e70c9e-0ace-48b9-a187-0c0003a5046f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ed08-f8e0-79f4-4eb5"},{"link_uuid":"c0a3f92b-5310-43b2-9c36-748c9534a94e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0b18-cddf-05fc-41b8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen store-interface files contain 61 audited prose blocks. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@d6669496cae4`; stable code and symbol anchors govern, while line ranges only identify immutable blobs.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only anchored comments and true leading docstrings in Scope. Preserve every non-docstring runtime string, constant, regex, fixture value, subprocess argument, decorator, assertion, and executable statement.\n\nParse immutable before/final blobs with `type_comments=True`; remove only allowlisted leading docstrings from modules, classes, functions, and async functions; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining ASTs to match. Restrict comment edits to anchored blocks and adjacent blank lines. Compare directives, inline comments, and shebangs byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n- `sync_contention_harness.py` module docstring — retain the shared harness, `_clear_sync_throttle`, and bare-import fixture topology.\n- `test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py` module docstring — retain atomic publication, no-debris behavior, and interruption at the write-lock boundary.\n- `test_event_append_transient_retry.py` module; three stderr-constant blocks; and retry/healing docstrings — retain classifier signatures and pre/post-ref retry boundaries.\n- `test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` named docstring and blocks bound to cache/proxy/provider stubs — retain optional-import isolation, keyword-only mode, ambient-proxy isolation, and provider-session behavior.\n- `test_git_contention_9305.py` module and concurrent-process docstrings — retain local-lock absorption, pathspec commits, and the two-process observable.\n- `test_inline_write_push.py` module and detached-upkeep docstrings — retain inline-writer inventory and the no-detached-mutator precondition.\n- `test_llm_optionality.py` module, `_gate_source_local`, operation/fail-safe blocks, named docstrings, and anchored fixture/assertion blocks — retain lazy imports, local-source necessity, raised versus structured degradation, exhaustive discovery, and childless seed reachability.\n- `test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py` module, `GateCheckingRunner`, and fanout docstrings — retain explicit gate-context propagation into raw threads.\n- `test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py` module docstring — retain repo-global stash semantics, interleaving race, SHA-addressed restore, and unchanged `refs/stash`.\n- `test_reads_under_sync_contention.py` module, deadline comments, named docstrings, and hang-guard blocks — retain complete-or-loud reads and distinct in-process/subprocess bounds.\n- `test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py` module and fetch-ref docstrings — retain full-history merge and destination refspecs.\n- `test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py` module docstring and comment bound to `runtime = reconcile._runtime` — retain one composed runtime, transport forwarding, and patching the exact module resolved by `reconcile`; preserve the dual-copy non-editable-install rationale.\n- `test_reconciler_apply_bindings_engine_identity.py` module, `restore_sys_modules` and split-engine test docstrings, plus the comment before reseeding canonical `rebar_reconciler` keys — retain the manufactured dual-install identity split, mandatory cache restoration, alternate-copy seed, and observable transport oracle. Preserve `_ORACLE`, copied-engine layout, `sys.modules` mutation, assertions, and the concise `__pycache__` exclusion comment.\n- `test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py` module docstring — retain public seam, frozen scope, selected-provider construction, transport seam, and secret boundaries.\n- `test_review_as_workflow.py` module docstring — retain executor bridging and all active equivalence/public-entry nodes.\n- `test_review_regressions.py` module docstring — retain rollback, index cleanup, and tracker-root consistency.\n- `test_show_no_stall.py` module and one-round burst block — retain short reconverge deadline, complete-or-error result, and detection-floor rationale.\n- `test_txn_transient_retry.py` module docstring — retain pre-ref `could not parse HEAD` retry and immediate non-transient failure.\n\nConsumers include pytest; store fixtures and contention suites; workflow/optionality CI; reconciler shape checks; documentation; and `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`. No runtime docstring reader was found.\n\nPreserve `type: ignore` directives on `GateCheckingRunner.run` and `test_dirty_merge_recovery_ignores_a_foreign_stash`, all other directives/inline comments, and every runtime string byte-for-byte.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the 61 scoped comments, true leading docstrings, or adjacent blank lines change; normalized AST equality passes.\n- [ ] Runtime values, assertions, decorators, executable statements, inline comments, and directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and removes repetition, history, ornament, or obvious narration.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per edited block with immutable before/final citations, preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, and both verdicts.\n- [ ] All 61 rows record `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Normalized and directive guards, exact paths, focused tests, comment hygiene, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized-AST/directive comparator; all 18 impacted files plus both preview-bound contention consumer nodes; comment hygiene; exact-path and diff checks; and `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_optionality.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_review_regressions.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_txn_transient_retry.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings_engine_identity.py","reason":"Condense split-engine identity-test prose while preserving module-cache restoration and the alternate-install transport oracle."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2d43-3c39-307e-4450"],["relates_to","0b18-cddf-05fc-41b8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","parent_status_uuid":"7a050883-6bce-4e96-a5e9-6ea940369c80","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"7788-7607-ecad-42d9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/interfaces/store","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import ast, subprocess, sys\nowners=(ast.Module,ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)\ndef norm(ref,path):\n source=subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{ref}:{path}\"],text=True)\n tree=ast.parse(source,type_comments=True)\n for node in ast.walk(tree):\n  if isinstance(node,owners) and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value,str):\n   node.body=node.body[1:]\n for item in tree.type_ignores:\n  item.lineno=0\n return ast.dump(tree,include_attributes=False)\nbad=[p for p in sys.argv[1:] if norm(\"HEAD^\",p)!=norm(\"HEAD\",p)]\nassert not bad,f\"normalized AST changed: {bad}\"' tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_optionality.py tests/interfaces/store/test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py tests/interfaces/store/test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_regressions.py tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py tests/interfaces/store/test_txn_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings_engine_identity.py","dd_id":"semantic","dd_text":"Prove executable Python semantics are unchanged after removing true leading docstrings and normalizing only type-ignore line numbers."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import re, subprocess, sys\npat=re.compile(r\"#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma\\b|fmt\\b|nosec\\b)\",re.I)\ndef directives(ref,path):\n lines=subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{ref}:{path}\"],text=True).splitlines()\n out=[]\n for i,line in enumerate(lines):\n  if not pat.search(line):\n   continue\n  nxt=next((x for x in lines[i+1:] if x.strip() and not x.lstrip().startswith(\"#\")),\"<EOF>\")\n  out.append((line,nxt))\n return out\nbad=[p for p in sys.argv[1:] if directives(\"HEAD^\",p)!=directives(\"HEAD\",p)]\nassert not bad,f\"directive text or attachment changed: {bad}\"' tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_optionality.py tests/interfaces/store/test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py tests/interfaces/store/test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_regressions.py tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py tests/interfaces/store/test_txn_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings_engine_identity.py","dd_id":"directives","dd_text":"Preserve directive text and attachment to the same following code."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import subprocess, sys\nexpected=set(sys.argv[1:])\nactual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^\",\"HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines())\nassert actual==expected,f\"changed paths mismatch: missing={sorted(expected-actual)} extra={sorted(actual-expected)}\"' tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py tests/interfaces/store/test_atomic_ticket_dir_create_021d.py tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_optionality.py tests/interfaces/store/test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py tests/interfaces/store/test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py tests/interfaces/store/test_review_regressions.py tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py tests/interfaces/store/test_txn_transient_retry.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings_engine_identity.py","dd_id":"paths","dd_tex